@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+id: dl-002-inject-task-timestamps-at-the-api-boundary
+type: decision-log
+title: "Inject task timestamps at the API boundary"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Tasks must expose ISO-8601 creation and modification times. Domain rules prohibit wall-clock access
+under `src/domain/`, while tests must remain deterministic.
+
+## Decision
+
+The public API supplies the current time to the task-list domain operations. The task list passes that
+value to task creation and successful mutations. The public API's time source is controllable so tests
+can assert exact timestamps without reading the real clock.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The domain stays deterministic and has no wall-clock dependency. Consumers receive timestamps on all
+tasks, and tests can verify precisely which successful operations refresh `updatedAt`.
