@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+---
+id: task-002-add-task-creation-and-update-timestamps
+type: task
+title: "Add task creation and update timestamps"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+Add ISO-8601 `createdAt` and `updatedAt` values to every task returned by the public API.
+
+The timestamps are set identically when a task is created. Completing, reopening, renaming, tagging,
+and untagging a task refreshes `updatedAt`; reads, failed operations, and removal do not.
+
+Implemented the approved decision in `dl-002-inject-task-timestamps-at-the-api-boundary`: the public API
+obtains time through an optional date provider and passes ISO-8601 timestamps into domain operations.
+Task creation reads the provider once and uses the same value for both fields. Successful mutations
+preserve creation time and refresh modification time, including accepted operations with unchanged
+titles or tags. The default provider reads the system clock outside the domain.
+
+Updated the README and API comments. No dependencies were added.
+
+## Verification
+
+Creation timestamps and modification timestamps for all five mutation types were classified as new
+behavior and tested red-first: the initial run failed three tests because timestamps were absent.
+Existing read, failure, removal, identity, and task-list behavior was characterized using a controlled
+clock. Additional edge coverage checks accepted operations with unchanged titles or tags.
+
+`npm test` passes all 16 tests. `git diff --check` passes.
